  "Text": "Whereas, Pursuant to Chapter 4 of Title 25 of the Administrative Code of the City of New York or the predecessor of such Chapter (the \"BID Law\"), the City established the 34th Street, 82nd Street, East Mid-Manhattan, Myrtle Avenue Brooklyn, Bay Ridge 5th Avenue, Southern Boulevard, Greater JFK, and West Village Business Improvement Districts in the City of New York; and\t\nWhereas, Pursuant to Local Law No. 82 for the year 1990, the City Council assumed responsibility for adopting legislation relating to Business Improvement Districts; and\nWhereas, Pursuant to Subdivision (b) of Section 25-410 of the BID Law, an increase in the amount to be expended annually may be adopted by local law, provided that the City Council determines, after a public hearing, that it is in the public interest to authorize the increase and that the tax and debt limits prescribed in Section 25-412 of the BID Law will not be exceeded; and\nWhereas, Eight Business Improvement Districts wish to increase the amount to be expended annually beginning on July 1, 2027, as follows: the 34th Street Business Improvement District, $16,300,000; 82nd Street Business Improvement District, $354,450; East Mid-Manhattan Business Improvement District, $6,000,000; Myrtle Avenue Brooklyn Business Improvement District, $775,000; Bay Ridge 5th Avenue Business Improvement District, $600,000; Southern Boulevard Business Improvement District, $600,000; Greater JFK Business Improvement District, $800,000; and the West Village Business Improvement District, $1,400,000; and \nWhereas, Pursuant to Subdivision (b) of Section 25-410 of the BID Law, the City Council is required to give notice of the public hearing by publication of a notice in at least one newspaper having general circulation in the districts specifying the time when and the place where the hearing will be held and stating the proposed amount to be expended annually; now, therefore, be it\nResolved, That the Council of the City of New York, pursuant to Subdivision (b) of Section 25-410 of the BID Law, hereby directs that:\n(i) November 19, 2026, is the date and the City Council Committee Room, 2nd Floor, City Hall is the place and 11:00AM is the time for a public hearing (the “Public Hearing”) to hear all persons interested in the legislation that would increase the amount to be expended annually in the 34th Street, 82nd Street, East Mid-Manhattan, Myrtle Avenue Brooklyn, Bay Ridge 5th Avenue, Southern Boulevard, Greater JFK, and West Village Business Improvement Districts; and\n(ii) On behalf of the City Council and pursuant to Subdivision (b) of Section 25-410 of the BID Law, the District Management Associations of the 34th Street, 82nd Street, East Mid-Manhattan, Myrtle Avenue Brooklyn, Bay Ridge 5th Avenue, Southern Boulevard, Greater JFK, and West Village Business Improvement Districts are hereby authorized to publish in a newspaper of general circulation in each district, not less than ten (10) days prior to the Public Hearing, a notice stating the time and place of the Public Hearing and setting forth the proposed increase in the amount to be expended annually in each of the eight Business Improvement Districts.",
  "RTF": "{\\rtf1\\fbidis\\ansi\\ansicpg1252\\deff0\\deflang1033\\deflangfe1033{\\fonttbl{\\f0\\froman\\fprq2\\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\\f1\\froman\\fprq2\\fcharset0 CG Times;}}\n{\\colortbl ;\\red0\\green0\\blue0;}\n\\viewkind4\\uc1\n\\v0\\par\nBy Council Member \\expndtw0 Lee\\expndtw-3\\par\n\\pard\\ltrpar\\nowidctlpar\\hyphpar0\\qj\\tx5310\\tab\\par\n\\pard\\ltrpar\\nowidctlpar\\fi720\\sl480\\slmult1\\qj Whereas, Pursuant to Chapter 4 of Title 25 of the Administrative Code of the City of New York or the predecessor of such Chapter (the \"BID Law\"), the City established the 34th Street, \\expndtw0 82nd Street, East Mid-Manhattan, Myrtle Avenue Brooklyn, Bay Ridge 5th Avenue, Southern Boulevard, Greater JFK, and West Village Business Improvement Districts in the City of New York; and\\expndtw-3\\tab\\par\n\\pard\\ltrpar\\nowidctlpar\\hyphpar0\\fi720\\sl480\\slmult1\\qj\\tx1440 Whereas, Pursuant to Local Law No. 82 for the year 1990, the City Council assumed responsibility for adopting legislation relating to Business Improvement Districts; and\\par\nWhereas, Pursuant to Subdivision (b) of Section 25-410 of the BID Law, an increase in the amount to be expended annually may be adopted by local law, provided that the City Council determines, after a public hearing, that it is in the public interest to authorize the increase and that the tax and debt limits prescribed in Section 25-412 of the BID Law will not be exceeded; and\\expndtw0\\par\n\\pard\\ltrpar\\nowidctlpar\\fi720\\sl480\\slmult1\\qj\\expndtw-3 Whereas,\\cf1\\expndtw0  Eight Business Improvement Districts wish to increase the amount to be expended annually beginning on July 1, 2027, as follows: the \\cf0 34th Street Business Improvement District, $16,300,000; 82nd Street Business Improvement District, $354,450; East Mid-Manhattan Business Improvement District, $6,000,000; Myrtle Avenue Brooklyn Business Improvement District, $775,000; Bay Ridge 5th Avenue Business Improvement District, $600,000; Southern Boulevard Business Improvement District, $600,000; Greater JFK Business Improvement District, $800,000; and the West Village Business Improvement District, $1,400,000; and \\expndtw-3\\par\n\\pard\\ltrpar\\nowidctlpar\\hyphpar0\\fi720\\sl480\\slmult1\\qj\\tx1440\\tx2430 Whereas, Pursuant to Subdivision (b) of Section 25-410 of the BID Law, the City Council is required to give notice of the public hearing by publication of a notice in at least one newspaper having general circulation in the districts specifying the time when and the place where the hearing will be held and stating the proposed amount to be expended annually; now, therefore, be it\\par\n\\pard\\ltrpar\\nowidctlpar\\hyphpar0\\fi720\\sl480\\slmult1\\qj\\tx1440 Resolved, That the Council of the City of New York, pursuant to Subdivision (b) of Section 25-410 of the BID Law, hereby directs that:\\par\n(i) November 19, 2026, is the date and the City Council Committee Room, 2nd Floor, City Hall\\-\\- is the place and 11:00AM is the time for a public hearing (the \\ldblquote Public Hearing\\rdblquote ) to hear all persons interested in the legislation that would increase the amount to be expended annually in the 34th Street, \\expndtw0 82nd Street, East Mid-Manhattan, Myrtle Avenue Brooklyn, Bay Ridge 5th Avenue, Southern Boulevard, Greater JFK, and West Village Business Improvement Districts; and\\expndtw-3\\par\n(ii) On\\expndtw0  behalf of the City Council and pursuant to Subdivision (b) of Section 25-410 of the BID Law, the District Management Associations of the 34th Street, 82nd Street, East Mid-Manhattan, Myrtle Avenue Brooklyn, Bay Ridge 5th Avenue, Southern Boulevard, Greater JFK, and West Village Business Improvement Districts are hereby authorized to publish in a newspaper of general circulation in each district, not less than ten (10) days prior to the Public Hearing, a notice stating the time and place of the Public Hearing and setting forth the proposed increase in the amount to be expended annually in each of the eight Business Improvement Districts.\\expndtw-3\\par\n\\pard\\ltrpar\\nowidctlpar\\expndtw0\\par\n}\n",
